      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel such intense pressure to maintain a certain standard of self-worth. However, quitting out of fear often means accepting an outcome that is more limiting than the struggle itself. Instead of viewing this as the end, consider it a necessary pause for reinvention, a critical part of an artist's journey. Your dignity is rooted in your authentic effort, not just in the quality of the output compared to your past self.",
      "source": "target",
